the kit's own reuse-checked commands pin `LC_ALL=C` when they start, and
@@NEW
functions run under an explicit `bash`, `LANG` and the locale categories
change no record the harness writes (it runs its own parsing under
`LC_ALL=C`, which decodes every byte and reads every ASCII grammar the kit
writes as any other locale would, and a parse that fails never reads as a
passing result), while a check whose programs read them pins them or declares
them, as the kit's own reuse-checked commands pin `LC_ALL=C` when they start;
the harness gives the caller's `LC_ALL` back to the command a capture runs,
and hashes a declared `LC_ALL` by that value, and
@@END
